#{[{:activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162974} :activity/id #uuid "9110c851-c32a-57df-a77a-329797a3df41" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048731 :topic/id #uuid "b99b224f-8118-53d5-8d6e-c47785040b57" :topic/math-academy-id 3028} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162971 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162056 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161856 :question/id #uuid "01fc4e2e-d93f-50b3-859e-19732d4f10c2" :question/math-academy-id "e-9111"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "405984cd-1e1b-54c6-bc75-268e127b9812" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050327}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162262} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162263} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186369036} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186369043} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186369050} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186369057} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420136} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420139}] :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Variance of a Constant"} :step/id #uuid "3174d04a-7e8e-5098-91d3-c55afedd2e39" :step/math-academy-id 33959 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162975}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162972 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162057 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161857 :question/id #uuid "a3f88c0e-9426-50d2-baf0-95909e222d4b" :question/math-academy-id "e-9112"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8a3752a0-431d-5520-97b1-493c36bbce54" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162264} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162266} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186369064} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186369071} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186369644} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186369651} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186369658} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186380524} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186380789} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420140} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186425506}] :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Variance of a Scaled Random Variable"} :step/id #uuid "fe3d0b73-cb7e-5370-9455-c490da334890" :step/math-academy-id 33961 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162976}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162973 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162058 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161858 :question/id #uuid "c20c7b15-e967-52a9-846d-4915f6661158" :question/math-academy-id "e-9114"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "85388f7d-b2ee-520b-b711-a7721c6f620c" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162265} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162267} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186244227} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186369078} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186369665} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186369672} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186369679} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186380531} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186380538} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186380796} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420137} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420138} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186425505}] :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Variance of a Transformed Random Variable"} :step/id #uuid "09f12104-7949-5867-9884-48e422a32857" :step/math-academy-id 33963 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162977}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162974 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186163273 :tutorial/content "There are several important properties of the variance of a random variable that we can use to simplify expressions. \n\nFirstly, the variance of a constant is always zero. That is, for any constant $a,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Var}[a] = 0.\n$$\n\nIntuitively, this makes sense. A constant does not vary, so the mean deviation from its expected value should be zero." :tutorial/id #uuid "6eb17ec7-1e57-5d75-8a71-9030a420602b" :tutorial/math-academy-id 5458 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "65bbda75-37ec-5809-926a-0fb8d31c008d" :step/math-academy-id 33964 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162971}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162975 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186163274 :tutorial/content "Suppose that $X$ is a random variable and $a$ is a constant. Then,\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Var}[aX] = a^2\\textrm{Var}[X].\n$$\n\nSo, for example, if we know that $\\textrm{Var}[X] = 2,$ then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[3X] & ={3}^{2}\\cdot \\text{Var}[X] \\\\  & =9\\cdot \\text{Var}[X] \\\\  & =9\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =18.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimilarly,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[-4X] & =(-4)^{2}\\cdot \\text{Var}[X] \\\\  & =16\\cdot \\text{Var}[X] \\\\  & =16\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =32.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Note:** To understand why we have to square the constant when we factor it outside the variance, it's helpful to remember that the variance is defined as the expected *squared* deviation from the mean:\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Var}[X] = \\textrm E [ (X - \\textrm E[X])^2 ]\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[aX] & =\\text{E}[(aX-\\text{E}[aX])^{2}] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[(aX-a\\text{E}[X])^{2}] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[{a}^{2}(X-\\text{E}[X])^{2}] \\\\  & ={a}^{2}\\text{E}[(X-\\text{E}[X])^{2}] \\\\  & ={a}^{2}\\text{Var}[X].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "d33b6982-066e-5c82-8138-0283ad8dccbb" :tutorial/math-academy-id 5459 :tutorial/title "The Variance of a Scaled Random Variable"} :step/id #uuid "55f9fd86-1f4a-5f2c-b7c2-a60113a4a9e8" :step/math-academy-id 33966 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162972}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162976 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186163275 :tutorial/content "Suppose that $X$ is a random variable and $a$ and $b$ are constants. It can be shown that\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Var}[aX+b] = a^2\\textrm{Var}[X].\n$$\n\nA proof of this result is given at the end of this lesson.\n\nTherefore, when a random variable is scaled by a factor of $a$ and shifted by a constant $b\\mathbin{:}$ \n\n- the variance is scaled by a factor of $a^2$ as before, and\n\n- the variance is unaffected by the shift.\n\nThe fact that shifting a random variable leaves the variance unaltered makes intuitive sense. Shifting all values of $X$ by a fixed amount does not change how far apart those values are from each other. \n\nFor example, if we know that $\\textrm{Var}[X] = 3,$ then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[2X+1] & ={2}^{2}\\cdot \\text{Var}[X] \\\\  & ={2}^{2}\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =4\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "1523e51b-84da-5100-809f-09fbcb0d80ba" :tutorial/math-academy-id 5460 :tutorial/title "The Variance of a Transformed Random Variable"} :step/id #uuid "e17beec2-91ed-5375-9c58-ab279784f2bf" :step/math-academy-id 33968 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162973}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162977 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186163276 :tutorial/content "We wish to prove the following result:\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Var}[aX+b] = a^2\\textrm{Var}[X]\n$$\n\nRecall that, by definition,\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Var}[X] = \\textrm E [ (X - \\textrm E[X])^2 ].\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[aX+b] & =\\text{E}[(aX+b-\\text{E}[aX+b])^{2}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the properties of expected value, we can simplify this as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[(aX+b-\\text{E}[aX+b])^{2}] & =\\text{E}[(aX+b-a\\text{E}[X]-b)^{2}] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[(aX-a\\text{E}[X])^{2}] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[(a(X-\\text{E}[X]))^{2}] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[{a}^{2}(X-\\text{E}[X])^{2}] \\\\  & ={a}^{2}\\text{E}[(X-\\text{E}[X])^{2}] \\\\  & ={a}^{2}\\text{Var}[X]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "0372f0de-b6a6-58ee-8195-c04024e8f745" :tutorial/math-academy-id 5461 :tutorial/title "Proof of the General Formula"} :step/id #uuid "da23e59c-3020-5db2-8f5b-77675938bf0b" :step/math-academy-id 33969}] :activity/title "Properties of Variance for Discrete Random Variables" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186162181}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046659} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186425510} :activity/id #uuid "6f0ea926-98c1-508c-aafd-6b9334df01ce" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048731 :topic/id #uuid "b99b224f-8118-53d5-8d6e-c47785040b57" :topic/math-academy-id 3028} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186425507 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186425505 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e9447cf-647a-5fa5-b1b7-8ad767262b04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425493} {:answer/id #uuid "26c878c9-4005-5ffb-b62a-ccf12e7653a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425495} {:answer/id #uuid "84d7e9cc-2b46-5e49-827d-3dc43ec7a3fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425499} {:answer/id #uuid "a04fede6-c5e8-5346-92ee-0dfe50e7363c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425500} {:answer/id #uuid "a7e38c85-b6da-52ad-a873-fe8715cae083" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425501}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186425493} :answer-field/id #uuid "9be7f666-e571-52b8-923e-291edd79be24" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425503}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "2adf151d-6d7b-5aee-975a-4588dddc072c" :question/math-academy-id "q-109086" :question/problem "If $\\text{Var}[X]=18,$ calculate $\\text{Var}[\\frac{1}{3}X+1].$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that for any random variable $X$ and constants $a$ and $b,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[aX+b]={a}^{2}\\cdot \\text{Var}[X].\n$$\n\nIn our case, $a=\\frac{1}{3}$ and $b=1.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[\\frac{1}{3}X+1] & ={(\\frac{1}{3})}^{2}\\cdot \\text{Var}[X] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}\\cdot 18 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "0925688f-b14f-5497-b2f8-ef5577ee74ea" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186425511}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186425508 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162267 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "af8dce06-ec2e-54f0-8068-081d29a00d10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186158805} {:answer/id #uuid "f65b10d3-6570-596d-aef7-36a7d9e90bc7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "35" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186158806} {:answer/id #uuid "f8c1bb8e-9e55-5585-849e-6e82c2d6778c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{14}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186158807} {:answer/id #uuid "2866549e-9133-5ffd-b73b-2bb7a74f8397" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "70" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186158808} {:answer/id #uuid "4319aba1-1a6d-55f0-8649-0a11c8e26ddb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "65" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186158809}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186158808} :answer-field/id #uuid "96f5d0fa-e64f-5420-894c-9af20eb4994a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186158804}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "07dc96f1-44f9-56f8-847d-dfc0e5291318" :question/math-academy-id "q-108946" :question/problem "The probability distribution of the random variable $X$ is given below. Given that $\\text{E}[X]=7,$ calculate $\\text{Var}[2-5X].$ \n\n| $x$ | $5$ | $6$ | $9$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $\\frac{1}{5}$ | $\\frac{2}{5}$ | $\\frac{2}{5}$ |" :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "Recall that for any random variable $X$ and constants $a$ and $b,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[aX+b]={a}^{2}\\cdot \\text{Var}[X].\n$$\n\nIn our case, $a=-5$ and $b=2.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[2-5X] & =(-5)^{2}\\cdot \\text{Var}[X] \\\\  & =25\\cdot \\text{Var}[X].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can compute the variance of $X$ using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdditionally, we're given that $\\text{E}[X]=7.$ \n\nWe start by computing $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}].$ Summing up the products of each value of ${X}^{2}$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={5}^{2}\\cdot f(5)+{6}^{2}\\cdot f(6)+{9}^{2}\\cdot f(9) \\\\  & =25(\\frac{1}{5})+36(\\frac{2}{5})+81(\\frac{2}{5}) \\\\  & =\\frac{259}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{259}{5}-{7}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{259}{5}-49 \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[2-5X] & =25\\cdot \\text{Var}[X] \\\\  & =25\\cdot \\frac{14}{5} \\\\  & =14\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =70.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "1bca5d11-c663-5970-a2d7-41fbabf9a6af" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186425509}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186425509 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186425506 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ffc334f-bda6-5020-8972-7c141e811580" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425494} {:answer/id #uuid "2a01301e-2613-5381-a06c-9e16aa051fd8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425496} {:answer/id #uuid "3e1bb640-287c-5a4d-9809-a95f12e541cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425497} {:answer/id #uuid "559bb6ee-9e3b-59fc-b4ec-1934f445e465" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425498} {:answer/id #uuid "bea01d67-a086-5031-9b05-53086e759f6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425502}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186425496} :answer-field/id #uuid "ef907e56-83d3-5832-9059-ba2b6e97be1a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425504}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "6da9aedf-d051-5c8d-9ea5-b796001b82b1" :question/math-academy-id "q-109056" :question/problem "The probability distribution of the random variable $X$ is given below. Given that $\\text{E}[X]=2,$ calculate $\\text{Var}[\\sqrt{3}X].$ \n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $2$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ |" :question/worked-solution "Recall that for any random variable $X$ and constant $a,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[aX]={a}^{2}\\cdot \\text{Var}[X].\n$$\n\nIn our case, $a=\\sqrt{3}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[\\sqrt{3}X] & ={\\sqrt{3}}^{2}\\cdot \\text{Var}[X] \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\text{Var}[X].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can compute the variance of $X$ using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2}\n$$\n\nAdditionally, we're given that $\\text{E}[X]=2.$ \n\nWe start by computing $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}].$ Summing up the products of each value of ${X}^{2}$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={0}^{2}\\cdot f(0)+{2}^{2}\\cdot f(2)+{4}^{2}\\cdot f(4) \\\\  & =4\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}+16\\cdot \\frac{1}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{20}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{20}{3}-{2}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[\\sqrt{3}X] & =3\\cdot \\text{Var}[X] \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\frac{8}{3} \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "2775e72e-c277-5c4c-8f6b-b21b5d18a293" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186425507}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186425510 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162264 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bdc2e9bd-883b-53b3-9944-cfc609ec7c04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186158787} {:answer/id #uuid "1da0e3f6-cfb8-53e6-a30c-128f6ea47744" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186158788} {:answer/id #uuid "456a4994-4a3b-5692-99e8-a647708d7a6e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "64" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186158789} {:answer/id #uuid "4bc8dced-9c70-5f0e-a44a-554c2928171a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186158790} {:answer/id #uuid "57a37707-7dd6-55aa-bf77-c3c838e9d2a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186158791}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186158787} :answer-field/id #uuid "5a78dcdb-24b3-5b74-9b4c-2a39c0c6e272" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186158786}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "1375f84f-9c97-5d6b-9ab0-2b5843b7a89e" :question/math-academy-id "q-108936" :question/problem "If $\\text{Var}[X]=8,$ calculate $\\text{Var}[2X].$" :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "Recall that for any random variable $X$ and constant $a,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[aX]={a}^{2}\\cdot \\text{Var}[X].\n$$\n\nIn our case, $a=2.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[2X] & ={2}^{2}\\cdot \\text{Var}[X] \\\\  & =4\\cdot 8 \\\\  & =32.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "53444b7f-e4a7-573c-87a7-c9522567fb10" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186425508}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186425511 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420137 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "37f0111e-003f-5538-a3b8-ed1430d08fdc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420111} {:answer/id #uuid "a0f2c3dd-df0a-57f1-9b19-b251ffe9a72e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420122} {:answer/id #uuid "bc26c2f9-39d9-5339-a3e8-be5d2e945ea8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420123} {:answer/id #uuid "c6d13b79-c01f-5ddb-888f-f826b5a1451c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420124} {:answer/id #uuid "e83e0132-215d-5133-98be-6554e8873e9a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420128}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420128} :answer-field/id #uuid "7d0a832f-24dd-571f-b252-8ec9cfdfbd85" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420134}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "12feee0e-318a-5930-8eca-dd111ec7b1c2" :question/math-academy-id "q-109091" :question/problem "The probability distribution of the random variable $X$ is given below. Given that $\\text{E}[X]=1,$ calculate $\\text{Var}[\\frac{1}{8}-\\frac{1}{2}X].$ \n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ |" :question/worked-solution "Recall that for any random variable $X$ and constants $a$ and $b,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[aX+b]={a}^{2}\\cdot \\text{Var}[X].\n$$\n\nIn our case, $a=-\\frac{1}{2}$ and $b=\\frac{1}{8}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[\\frac{1}{8}-\\frac{1}{2}X] & ={(-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}\\cdot \\text{Var}[X] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot \\text{Var}[X].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can compute the variance of $X$ using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2}\n$$\n\nAdditionally, we're given that $\\text{E}[X]=1.$ \n\nWe start by computing $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}].$ Summing up the products of each value of ${X}^{2}$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={0}^{2}\\cdot f(0)+{1}^{2}\\cdot f(1)+{3}^{2}\\cdot f(3) \\\\  & =1\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}+9\\cdot \\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}-{1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[\\frac{1}{8}-\\frac{1}{2}X] & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot \\text{Var}[X] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot \\frac{3}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "e8ab5da7-93a7-56c3-964a-5c487de36ed5"}] :activity/title "Properties of Variance for Discrete Random Variables" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425492}]}
